---
title: decode_receipt (Osaka blocks.py)
---
stateDiagram-v2
    direction TB

    [*] --> q_init
    q_init --> q_check_type : isinstance(receipt, Bytes)
    q_check_type --> q_validate : receipt is Bytes
    q_check_type --> q_return_as_is : receipt is not Bytes
    q_validate --> q_decode : assert receipt[0] in (1, 2, 3, 4)
    q_decode --> q_final : return rlp.decode_to(Receipt, receipt[1:])
    q_return_as_is --> q_final : return receipt
    q_final --> [*]

    note right of q_validate
        INV: If receipt is Bytes, first byte must be in {1, 2, 3, 4}
    end note

    note right of q_decode
        INV: decode_receipt is the inverse of encode_receipt
        for all transaction types
    end note

    note right of q_return_as_is
        INV: Non-Bytes receipts (LegacyTransaction)
        are returned unchanged
    end note
